@startuml libtetrissh_secure_session

!theme plain

skinparam backgroundColor #FFF9FC
skinparam defaultFontName "Avenir Next"
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #756A83
  ArrowThickness 1.6
  ParticipantBorderColor #8B7E9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantFontColor #40364D
  LifeLineBorderColor #C8BFD3
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F3EDF7
  NoteBorderColor #9FC5A7
  NoteBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  NoteFontColor #3F6848
  DividerBackgroundColor #F0E7FA
  DividerBorderColor #B69ACF
  DividerFontColor #604978
}

title <size:22><b>tetriSH Secure Connection</b></size>\n<size:14>A simple view of the libtetrissh handshake</size>

participant "Game Client\n(tetrisu)" as Client #DDF3F5
participant "Client Security\n(libtetrissh)" as ClientSSH #DFF3E4
participant "Server Security\n(libtetrissh)" as ServerSSH #E9E2F7
participant "Game Server\n(tetrisd)" as Server #F9E2DC

== 1. Connect ==

Client -> Server: Open TCP connection
Server -> ServerSSH: Start secure handshake
Client -> ClientSSH: Start secure handshake

== 2. Verify server and share a key ==

ClientSSH -> ServerSSH: Fresh random nonce
ServerSSH --> ClientSSH: Server certificate
ServerSSH --> ClientSSH: Signed nonce (RSA-PSS)
ClientSSH -> ClientSSH: Verify certificate and signature
ClientSSH -> ServerSSH: Encrypted AES-256 session key (RSA-OAEP)
ServerSSH -> ServerSSH: Decrypt and store session key

note over ClientSSH, ServerSSH
Secure session established
end note

== 3. Play over the encrypted session ==

Client -> ClientSSH: HTTTP game command
ClientSSH -> ServerSSH: AES-256 encrypted frame
ServerSSH -> Server: Decrypted HTTTP command
Server -> ServerSSH: HTTTP response / game state
ServerSSH -> ClientSSH: AES-256 encrypted frame
ClientSSH -> Client: Decrypted response / game state

note over Client, Server #FFF3CD
All HTTTP traffic is encrypted after the handshake.
The server remains authoritative over game state.
end note

@enduml
